### Transition Timing: Quick vs. Gradual

Same blend, two durations. A 0.1-second crossfade feels snappy; a 2-second fade feels contemplative.

```scheme
(define (blend-x ax bx w)
  (+ (* ax (- 1.0 w))
     (* bx w)))

(motion
 (at 0.0
     (pose
      (entity 'disc
              (transform
               (blend-x 50.0 250.0 0.0)
               100.0
               0.0))))
 (at 0.1
     (pose
      (entity 'disc
              (transform
               (blend-x 50.0 250.0 1.0)
               100.0
               0.0)))))
```

[VISUAL: Disc snaps from left to right in a tenth of a second.]

Same blend, but stretched: the disc will now cover the same distance across a two-second span. Watch the pacing change, not the endpoints.

```scheme
(define (blend-x ax bx w)
  (+ (* ax (- 1.0 w))
     (* bx w)))

(motion
 (at 0.0
     (pose
      (entity 'disc
              (transform
               (blend-x 50.0 250.0 0.0)
               100.0
               0.0))))
 (at 2.0
     (pose
      (entity 'disc
              (transform
               (blend-x 50.0 250.0 1.0)
               100.0
               0.0)))))
```

[VISUAL: Disc drifts slowly from left to right over two seconds.]

The endpoints are identical to the snappy version—only the duration between them changed. Duration turns snap into drift; the blend formula stays put.

---


### Blending Rotation Shortest-Path

Linear blend of angles can spin the long way. Wrap angle difference to `[-180, 180]` first.

```scheme
(define (angle-diff a b)
  (let ((d (- b a)))
    (cond
     ((> d 180.0) (- d 360.0))
     ((< d -180.0) (+ d 360.0))
     (else d))))

(define (blend-angle ax bx w)
  (+ ax (* (angle-diff ax bx) w)))

(motion
 (pose
  (entity 'arrow
          (transform
           150.0
           150.0
           (blend-angle 10.0 350.0 0.5)))))
```

At `w=0.5`, angle is `0.0` (halfway on the short arc from 10° to 350°), not `180.0`.

[VISUAL: Arrow points north, having rotated -10° instead of +170°.]

