### Crossfade Two Oscillators with Different Amplitude

Blend isn't just for positions—it works on the *values feeding* a position too. Here we crossfade between a gentle swing and a wide swing so the pendulum grows over time.

```scheme
(define (osc-small t)
  (* 10.0 (sin (* 5.0 t))))

(define (osc-large t)
  (* 40.0 (sin (* 5.0 t))))

(define (blend-x ax bx w)
  (+ (* ax (- 1.0 w))
     (* bx w)))

(motion
 (at 0.0
     (pose
      (entity 'pendulum
              (transform
               100.0
               (+ 100.0 (blend-x (osc-small 0.0) (osc-large 0.0) 0.0))
               0.0))))
 (at 1.0
     (pose
      (entity 'pendulum
              (transform
               100.0
               (+ 100.0 (blend-x (osc-small 1.0) (osc-large 1.0) 0.5))
               0.0))))
 (at 2.0
     (pose
      (entity 'pendulum
              (transform
               100.0
               (+ 100.0 (blend-x (osc-small 2.0) (osc-large 2.0) 1.0))
               0.0)))))
```

[VISUAL: Pendulum swing amplitude grows smoothly from 10 to 40 pixels.]

The oscillation frequency stays constant; only its size changes. Blending the two amplitude sources is what makes the growth feel smooth instead of stepped.

